EGMO-2017-notes.pdf,2,"Find the smallest positive integer k for which there exists a coloring of the positive
integers Z>0 with k colors and a function f : Z>0 \toZ>0 with the following two
properties:
(i) For all positive integers m, n of the same color, f(m + n) = f(m) + f(n).
(ii) There are positive integers m, n such that f(m + n) ̸= f(m) + f(n).","Answer: k = 3.
Construction for k = 3: let
