f(a)2 + f(b)2 + f(c)2 = 2f(a)f(b) + 2f(b)f(c) + 2f(c)f(a).","Answer: for arbitrary k \inZ, we have
(i) f(x) = kx2,
(ii) f(x) = 0 for even x, and f(x) = k for odd x, and
(iii) f(x) = 0 for x \equiv0 (mod 4), f(x) = k for odd x, and f(x) = 4k for x \equiv2 (mod 4).
These can be painfully seen to work. (It's more natural to think of these as f(x) = x2,
