-- g(4) = 0, then we get (g(n))n\ge0 = (0, 1, 2, 1, 0, 1, 2, 1, . . . ). This works.
-- g(4) = 4k. This only happens when g(1) = k, g(2) = 2k, g(3) = 3k, g(4) = 4k.
Then
*g(5) = \pm3k \pm 2k = \pm4k \pm k.
