web.evanchen.cc, updated 31 December 2025","Claim --- Given a 4-regular multigraph on n vertices (where self-loops are allowed
and have degree 2), one can color the edges blue and green such that each vertex
has two blue and two green edges.
Proof. Each connected component of the graph can be decomposed into an Eulerian
circuit, since 4 is even. A connected component with k vertices has 2k edges in its
Eulerian circuit, so we may color the edges in this circuit alternating green and blue.
This may be checked to work.
