IMO-2020-notes.pdf,6,"Consider an integer n > 1, and a set S of n points in the plane such that the distance
between any two different points in S is at least 1. Prove there is a line \ellseparating
S such that the distance from any point of S to \ellis at least \Omega(n-1/3).
