k = \lfloorlog2(n)\rfloor+ 1.
The following short solution was posted at https://aops.com/community/p28134004, ap-
parently first found by the team leader for Iran.
We construct a rooted binary tree T1 on the set of all circles as follows. For each row,
other than the bottom row:
{\textbullet} Connect the red circle to both circles under it;
{\textbullet} White circles to the left of the red circle in its row are connected to the left;
{\textbullet} White circles to the right of the red circle in its row are connected to the right.
The circles in the bottom row are all leaves of this tree.
