IMO-2024-notes.pdf,3,"Let a1, a2, a3, . . . be an infinite sequence of positive integers, and let N be a positive
integer. Suppose that, for each n > N, the number an is equal to the number
of times an-1 appears in the list (a1, a2, . . . , an-1). Prove that at least one of the
sequences a1, a3, a5, . . . and a2, a4, a6, . . . is eventually periodic.
We present the solution from ""gigamilkmen'tgeg"" in https://aops.com/community/p31224483,
with some adaptation from the first shortlist official solution as well.
