{\textparagraph} Counting.
Back to the main problem. The point is that we need to find the number
of up-right paths for which the two resulting regions have equal numbers of black and
white squares; call such paths balanced. Since the overall 2m \times 2n grid has 2mn black
and 2mn white squares, it's sufficient for just the bottom-right staircase to have equal
black and white cells.
Then in general, an up-right path is characterized by integer sequences
