ith column, for i = 1, . . . , 2n, has (i) one more black square than white if hi is odd and
i \equiv1 (mod 2); (ii) one more white square than black if hi is odd and i \equiv0 (mod 2); (iii)
equal black and white squares if hi is even. The conclusion follows immediately.
