\ell
During this process, we consider the set of points on the same side of \ellas C, and let x
be the number of such red points minus the number of such blue points. Note that:
{\textbullet} Every time \elltouches a blue point, x increases by 1.
{\textbullet} Every time \elltouches a red point, x decreases by 1.
{\textbullet} Initially, x = +1.
{\textbullet} Just before reaching the end we have x = -1.
