with center O, if we color A and O red but B and C blue, then no balancing line passes
through O.
On the other hand, in On the number of balanced lines, by J. Pach and R. Pinchasi,
(Discrete and Computational Geometry, 2001, p. 611-628) it is shown that in fact there are
at least n balancing lines.
