The curve \gamma by definition should cross y = x -1 at the point b = (1, 0). Let a denote
the first point of this sequence after p1 for which \gamma crosses y = x -1 again.
Now a is tiled by a vertical domino whose black point is to the right of \ell. But the line
segment \ellcuts Q into two parts, and the orientation of \gamma has this path also entering
from the right. This contradicts the fact that the orientation of \gamma points only from white
to black within dominoes. This contradiction completes the proof.
Remark. Note the problem is false if you allow holes (consider a 3 \times 3 with the middle
square deleted).
