Claim --- Apply a push-down preserves the main divisibility condition. Moreover,
it doesn't change A unless |v| = 50, where it decreases A by 50 instead.
Proof. The statement P(u) is only affected when u \subseteqv: to be precise, one term on the
right-hand side of P(u) decreases by |v|, while |v| -|u| terms increase by 1, for a net
change of -|u|. So P(u) still holds.
To see A doesn't change for |v| > 50, note |v| terms increase by 1 while one term
decreases by -|v|. When |v| = 50, only f(v) decreases by 50.
